# XSH puts()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.puts.001
anchor     functions/puts.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/puts.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       With standard output on a regular file, puts("hello") and then
           puts("") each return a non-negative value, and after
           fflush(stdout) the file holds exactly "hello\n\n".
note       Which non-negative value is open (APPLICATION USAGE); variants
           puts.returns_count and puts.returns_last.
test       t/001-writes.c

assertion  XSH.puts.002
anchor     functions/puts.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/fputc.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
says       With stdout made unbuffered and descriptor 1 then closed,
           puts("ab") returns EOF, sets errno to EBADF and sets the error
           indicator of stdout.
note       Where setvbuf() refuses _IONBF, the test writes until a call
           fails; if none does within 4 MiB the result is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/002-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.puts.003
anchor     functions/puts.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       With standard output on a regular file whose modification time
           is set to 2001-09-09, after puts("x") and a successful
           fflush(stdout), fstat() shows a later st_mtim.
note       As for XSH.fputc.005 (the change time is not checked).
test       t/003-mtime.c
